  "result": "All 8 tests pass (5 in test_t1, 3 in test_t2).\n\n**What I changed**\n\n- **ratelimit/limiter.py**: kept the token-bucket design and factored the refill math into a non-mutating helper that computes the tokens a key would hold at a given time. The `allow` method now uses that helper and writes the bucket back.\n- **`remaining(key, now)`** returns the integer part of the refilled token count. It never creates or mutates a bucket, so a fresh key reports its full limit.\n- **`reset(key)`** drops the key's bucket. Any per-key limit override stays in place, since resetting usage and changing configuration are separate concerns.\n- **`set_limit(key, limit)`** stores a per-key override used for both capacity and refill rate. The window is shared. If the key already holds more tokens than the new limit, they are clamped down. The override is validated the same way as the constructor limit.\n- **SPEC.md**: added the three new method signatures to the public interface block.\n\nOne judgment call worth noting. Whether `reset` should also clear a `set_limit` override was not specified. I chose to keep the override, so a VIP key that gets reset stays VIP.",
